---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { LAST_UPDATED, CLARITY_ID } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Cookies on Bridge to 59: none set, and how to check it yourself" description="Bridge to 59 sets no cookie and keeps nothing on your device: balances, ages and spending typed into the calculators stay in the open page. Here is how to verify it in your browser." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>This site sets no cookie and uses no local storage. The balances, ages and spending you type are computed inside the page and disappear when you close it, unless you copy a share link, which carries them in its address.</p>
    <h2>No banner, and why</h2>
    <p>A consent banner is required when a site stores or reads non-essential information on a device. Nothing of the kind happens here. {CLARITY_ID ? 'The stability monitoring described in the privacy policy runs without cookies and stores nothing on your device.' : 'No analytics, advertising or social script is loaded.'}</p>
    <h2>How to check</h2>
    <p>Open your browser's developer tools (F12), tab Application or Storage: Cookies and Local Storage stay empty while you use the calculators. The Network tab shows that changing a field sends nothing anywhere.</p>
    <p>See also the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
